+# AGENTS.md
+
+## Project overview
+
+This is a **custom fork of Chromium for Android** (SystemWebView/Chrome). Target is `target_os="android"`. The build is orchestrated by `build.sh` and `gn_domono_android.py`, which set custom GN args and call `autoninja`. This is NOT a standard Chromium checkout and does NOT use `gclient sync`.
+
+## Build
+
+Source `env.sh` first to set PATH and environment variables, then run `build.sh`.
+
+```sh
+source env.sh
+./build.sh --UseBuildId --symbols
+```
+
+### Common build targets
+
+| Target | Flag | Output dir |
+|--------|------|------------|
+| SystemWebView (default) | N/A | `out/DefaultSys` |
+| WebView SDK instrumentation | `--target_apk=webview_instrumentation_apk` | `out/webview_instrumentation_apk` |
+| Chrome Public APK | `--target_apk=chrome_public_apk` | `out/chrome_public_apk` |
+
+### Key build flags
+
+- `--domono_target_cpu=arm64|arm|x64|x86` – single ABI build
+- `--domono_64bit_only=true` – skip 32-bit secondary ABI
+- `--symbols` – archive unstripped .so files for debugging
+- `--UseBuildId` – stamp build ID from git commit hash
+- `--no-ccache` – disable ccache
+- `export XMAKE_WITH_ASAN=true` before `build.sh` – ASAN build
+- `--domono_is_hwasan=true` – HWASAN build (arm64 64-bit-only only)
+
+### Build process
+
+`build.sh` runs: `gn_domono_android.py` → `gn gen` → `autoninja` → strip + repackage APK.
+
+GN args are generated by `gn_domono_android.py:133`. Key defaults it sets:
+```
+is_debug=false, is_official_build=true, is_component_build=false
+treat_warnings_as_errors=false, symbol_level=1
+is_domono=true, target_os="android"
+```
+
+### GN / Ninja (manual)
+
+```sh
+source env.sh
+# Generate gn args manually:
+gn gen out/DefaultSys --args='target_os="android" target_cpu="arm64" is_debug=false'
+# Build a specific target:
+autoninja -j24 -C out/DefaultSys system_webview_apk
+```
+
+## Code style & formatting
+
+- C/C++: Chromium style via `.clang-format` + `.clang-tidy`. Use `clang-format -i` with the repo's `.clang-format` at root.
+- Python: `yapf` (config at root `.yapfignore`). Ignored third-party paths are listed there.
+- Rust: `rustfmt` via `.rustfmt.toml`
+- Python stub-generation bypass: `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` is set by `build.sh`.
+
+## Testing
+
+Tests are built and run through Ninja targets. Common test targets:
+- `base_unittests`, `content_unittests`, `net_unittests`, `components_unittests`
+- `android_webview/test:*` targets
+- Blink / WPT: `blink_web_tests`, `blink_wpt_tests`
+
+Run tests via Ninja and use gtests:
+```sh
+autoninja -C out/DefaultSys content_unittests && out/DefaultSys/content_unittests
+```
+
+## Project structure
+
+- `base/`, `content/`, `chrome/`, `android_webview/` – core Chromium layers
+- `v8/`, `third_party/blink/` – JavaScript engine and rendering engine
+- `android_webview/domono/` – Custom Domono shell APK code (`BUILD.gn:425`)
+- `init_tools/148/` – Custom depot_tools and build helpers
+- `agents/` – AI coding agent prompts and skills (Chromium upstream content)
+- `.claude/`, `.gemini/`, `.agents/` – Agent config dirs
+- `gn_domono_android.py` – GN arg generator
+- `env.sh` – Environment setup (PATH, SDK paths, etc.)
+
+## Important constraints
+
+- `treat_warnings_as_errors = false` – this is a fork-specific override; upstream has it true.
+- The `out/DefaultSys` directory name is hard-wired in `build.sh` for SCM tooling compatibility.
+- `is_domono=true` is set globally (used by GN conditionals, e.g. domono_shell_apk in `BUILD.gn:425`).
+- `build/util/LASTCHANGE` and `LASTCHANGE.committime` are pre-seeded by `build.sh` if missing.
+- JS/TS config: `tools/typescript/tsconfig_base.json` uses `module="NodeNext"`; the root `package.json` has `"type": "module"` to control module resolution.
+- **IRON RULE**: NEVER use `libstandalonelibwebviewchromium.so`. Only `libwebviewchromium.so` is allowed. The `libstandalonelibwebviewchromium` is a test-only library and must not be referenced in production code, BUILD.gn, or APK packaging.
+
+## Repository quirks
+
+- `git clone` is NOT how to set up this repo (see `README.md:8`). Source is obtained through depot_tools / custom processes.
+- This repo contains Google-internal submodules marked with `gclient-condition` in `.gitmodules`. Most agents will not have access to these.
+- The `DEPS` file is extensive (~4900 lines) managing all third-party dependencies via gclient.
+
+## Debugging & error reporting
+
+- When reporting build errors, compile failures, or crash locations, **always include the full absolute file path and line number**. Format: `/path/to/file.java:42`. Never use just a filename or relative path.
+- When referencing a crash from a tombstone, include the crash address offset and the symbol/function name if decoded.
+
+## Native crash analysis workflow
+
+When a native crash (SIGSEGV/SIGTRAP/SIGABRT) occurs in `libwebviewchromium.so`:
+
+1. **Get crash address from tombstone:**
+   ```sh
+   adb shell "head -20 /data/tombstones/tombstone_XX"
+   ```
+   Note `fault addr` and the first native frame offset (e.g. `#00 pc 0x7999b58`).
+
+2. **Decode address to source location using llvm-symbolizer:**
+   ```sh
+   SO=out/DefaultSys_arm64/android_clang_arm64_webview/lib.unstripped/libwebviewchromium.so
+   third_party/llvm-build/Release+Asserts/bin/llvm-symbolizer --obj="$SO" 0x7999b58
+   ```
+   This outputs: `function_name`, `file_path:line_number`, and the call stack leading to the crash.
+
+3. **Read the source code at the crash line to understand the CHECK/DCHECK failure.**
+
+4. **Report findings with full path and line number**, e.g.:
+   ```
+   Crash at /path/to/file.cc:119 — CHECK(data_pack->LoadFromFileRegion(...)) << "failed to load locale.pak"
+   ```
